course: dictionary
lesson: 4883
title: Idle: more than doing nothing
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Idle has more than one meaning, so read the words around it to find the right one. «The machines stood idle in the empty factory.» The clue is the empty factory: idle means not being used.
explain: Idle can also mean lazy, or not wanting to work. «Come and bear a hand, Rat, and don't stand about idle!» Bear a hand means help, so idle means doing nothing when you could be helping.
explain: Idle can be a verb too. An engine idles when a car is parked but still running. «Habits change slowly, with more to do than to sit about idle.» Here, to sit about idle means to sit around doing nothing. Try your meaning in the sentence: does «sit around doing nothing» still make sense? Then it is right.
fact: Idle is an adjective and a verb. As an adjective it means not being used, lazy, or without a real reason or purpose.
fact: «Idle» can mean without a real reason, as in «an idle threat».
fact: As a verb, to idle means to spend time doing nothing, or for an engine to run slowly while the car is not moving.
fact: Many schools have «no idling» signs because an idling car makes fumes.
fact: Phrases to know: stand idle, idle chatter, idle away the time.
exercise: «The machines stood idle in the empty factory.» What does idle mean here? | Very noisy | Painted bright red | *Not being used | Running fast
exercise: «Come and bear a hand, Rat, and don't stand about idle!» Bear a hand means help. What does idle suggest? | Being very quick | Going home early | *Doing nothing when help is needed | Helping with a big smile
exercise: «Habits change slowly: fewer friends who lead you into trouble and more things to do than to be idle.» What does idle mean here? | Going to school | Being brave | *Doing nothing | Playing games
test: Many schools have «no idling» signs. Why? | Because idling cars are too fast | Because idling cars are loud and fun | Because idling cars need new paint | *Because idling cars make fumes
test: Mum says «sit about idle». Which word is closest in meaning to idle? | Hungry | *Lazy | Quick | Loud
exam: Which phrase uses idle to mean without a real reason or purpose? | An idling engine | *An idle threat | Stand idle in the shed | Idle away the time on the sofa
